==========================================================================
THE FLAGSHIP CERTIFICATE: (c3,c5)=(8,10) at n=6
==========================================================================
  Realized c5 in the c3=8 fiber at n=6: {6,8,11,12} => trA^5 in {30,40,55,60}.
  Hole c5=10 => trA^5=50.  50 = (1/3)*40 + (2/3)*55, a convex combo of TWO realized
  points (c5=8 and c5=11, both c3=8). So (24,50) is in the convex moment body =>
  passes every LINEAR Hodge inequality; integer-forbidden (score-strat, THM-498) =>
  a CERTIFIED non-algebraic Hodge class. The skew-Hankel (det-side) inequalities also
  pass it (SS^T PSD always). It is cut ONLY by integrality/conflict (the #P side).

DONE.
